			<div class="content" id="post-content-4837000">
									

<p>I like the idea of both the paper itself, the use of cross-testing for actual research, and the &quot;conclusion&quot; it arrives at, but there are a few things that made me downvote:</p>
<ul>
<li>the size of the letters (this is the least important one)</li>
<li>Analyzing the documentation of SCP-173. This only makes sense out-of-universe. In-universe it would make more sense to frame this as an analysis of SCP-173's properties itself.</li>
<li>I think the writing could still be written a bit more clinical. It also didn't flow very well.</li>
<li>The paper makes a hypothesis at multiple points and then proceeds as if the hypothesis was proven fact. It would help a lot if more experimentation was done to support the hypothesis before moving on.</li>
<li>It would be better if the two theories at the end, quantum state and extradimensional control, were more aligned with each other. If they were more connected, it would feel more like &quot;everything adds up&quot; instead of a retroactive explanation for SCP-173. The quantum state theory adds a lot to these, as it really &quot;fits&quot; SCP-173 in a way. The extradimensional control theory, not so much.</li>
</ul>

							</div>

								
					
